==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*leyǵʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|lecherous}}, {{m|enm|licherous}}, from {{der|en|fro|*lecherous}} (attested in {{cog|fro|lecherousement|t=lecherously}}), from {{der|en|fro|lecherie}}, {{m|fro|licherie|t=gluttony, sensuality, lewdness, lechery}}, from {{der|en|fro|lecher}}, {{m|fro|lechier}}, {{m|fro|lekier}}, {{m|fro|lescher|t=to lick, live in gluttony or sensuality}}, from Old {{der|en|frk|*likkōn|*lekkōn, *likkōn|t=to lick}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*likkōną|t=to lick}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*leyǵʰ-|t=to lick}}, equivalent to {{suffix|en|lecher|ous}}. More at {{m|en|lick}}.

